> The secret to incredibly juicy Sheng Jian Bao is whipping the liquid into the minced pork. This technique, called 'da shui' (beating water), ensures the meat filling acts like a sponge, retaining all that delicious broth as it cooks inside the bun!

== Dough ==

In a large #bowl{}, mix @all-purpose flour{250%g}, @active dry yeast{1%tsp}, and @sugar{1%tsp} [- You can use instant yeast here as well, just mix it right in without blooming. -] 

Pour in @warm water{140%ml} little by little while stirring with a pair of chopsticks (or a fork). 

Then knead with your hand until a smooth, elastic dough forms. Cover the bowl with a wet kitchen towel. 

Leave to rise in a warm place until double in size. It will take between ~{40-90%minutes} depending on the room temperature.

== Filling ==

Put @minced pork{250%g} (ideally with some good fat content), @spring onion{2%tbsp}(finely chopped), @ginger{1/2%tbsp}(minced), @light soy sauce{2%tsp}, @sesame oil{1/2%tsp}, @salt{1/4%tsp}, and @ground Sichuan pepper{1%pinch} into a large #bowl{}.

Swirl constantly in the same direction while gradually adding @water{75%ml} (or @chicken stock{75%ml}) spoon by spoon into the mixture -- Keep stirring in one direction! This develops the proteins and helps the meat absorb the liquid for maximum juiciness.

== Shaping the Buns ==

Knead the dough on a floured work surface until it goes back to its original size -- This removes large air bubbles, ensuring your buns have a smooth surface after steaming.

Divide it into 20 equal portions. Roll each piece into a disk-like wrapper. 

Hold the wrapper in the palm of one hand. Place some filling in the middle. Use the other hand to fold the edge anticlockwise by pinching with your thumb and index finger until the bun is completely sealed.

Leave to rest for ~{15%minutes} before frying.

== Frying the Buns ==

Heat up @cooking oil{1%tbsp} in a #frying pan{} with a tight-fitting lid over high heat. Place in the buns.

When the bottom part becomes golden brown, pour in @water{240%ml} then cover with a lid -- Stand back as you pour, because the water will splatter aggressively when it hits the hot oil!

Uncover when the water evaporates completely. Sprinkle @toasted sesame seeds{1%tbsp} and @spring onion{1%tbsp}(finely chopped) over the buns. 

Cook for another ~{30%seconds} or so to re-crisp the bottoms, then serve immediately.

